From: Brady <brady@aioscilloscope.com>
Subject: drm/bridge: dw-hdmi: the CEC wake-up interrupt is optional, so ask for it as one
Copyright (C) 2026 Olympian LED, Inc.

The DesignWare HDMI probe looks for a second interrupt for CEC wake-up,
which most Rockchip HDMI blocks do not have, and the platform core logged
its absence as an error on every boot. Request it as an optional interrupt;
nothing else changes.

---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-hdmi.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-hdmi.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-hdmi.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-hdmi.c
@@ -5994,7 +5994,7 @@
 		cec.ops = &dw_hdmi_cec_ops;
 		cec.irq = irq;
 
-		irq = platform_get_irq(pdev, 1);
+		irq = platform_get_irq_optional(pdev, 1);
 		if (irq < 0)
 			dev_dbg(hdmi->dev, "can't get cec wake up irq\n");
 
